     1	# Why the fresh topics miss line 5 (D604's trace), 2026-11-16, $0
     2	
     3	`line5_trace.py` → `line5-trace-output.txt`. It reads the stored fresh reading (`poc/data/clean-fresh-a2-2026-11-16/choices/reading`)
     4	with the gate-1 scorer's own functions, for the control arm (the frozen step). It reproduces the recorded line 5: 2 of 5 right with
     5	unresolved points counted for the answer, 1 of 5 with them counted against.
     6	
     7	## Topic by topic
     8	
     9	| Topic (kind) | What blocks it, counted for / against | How settled | Reaches what a reader of the product sees? | Existing record |
    10	|---|---|---|---|---|
    11	| clean-14 (theme figure) | XR / XR | Passes 1 and 3: both third readers fail XR (the reference: IDC's "19% growth" forecast for a unit count). Pass 2 split. | **No.** No judging request, page or service reads the ladder's reference (`gate1-stick/RESULT.md`, re-checked: `bundle.py` reads only `not_judged`, `event`, `figure`). The reference only places the ranges, and X (ranges) holds on all 12 written control sends. | XR not read by the product; an event's reference has no bounded repair (D557, D558); "what counts as an expectation" is an open form issue. |
    12	| clean-15 (theme figure) | L, XR / L, XR | L: pass 1 both first readers; pass 2 both third readers; pass 3 split. XR: pass 1 both first readers. | **Yes, for L:** a part the question leaves out, now shown in the card's list of parts not judged. XR: no. | Line 2's class; no sourced main-part rule (D580); tuning stopped (D586, D391). |
    13	| clean-16 (AI bill) | none / none: three justified refusals | Both families: N holds. | Right. | |
    14	| clean-17 (event) | R, XR / R, XR | R: pass 3 both third readers (the wait-as-ruling-out class); pass 1 split. XR: all three passes, both first readers. | **Yes, for R:** the Ruled-out rung's words. XR: no (the judge never sees an event's reference, D557). | The postponement boundary, on Alex's page (D591). |
    15	| clean-18 (company figure) | none / D | D split on all three passes (Codex fails, Claude holds). | **Yes,** the due day is shown, and it is code's D414 day, 60 days after year-end. Readers who fail it read the request's fiscal-year note ("around 2027-02; use that day"), which contradicts code. | The reader discrepancy (D590): read alone, both families hold D on the class. The request-and-code contradiction (`universe.py:136` against D414) is recorded and not changed. |
    16	
    17	## What this gives
    18	
    19	- **On fresh topics, line 5's misses reduce to four recorded things:**
    20	  - a mark no reader of the product sees (XR, on 3 of 4 written topics, and the only blocker of clean-14);
    21	  - a stopped class (L);
    22	  - an unresolved policy boundary (R, Alex's);
    23	  - a reader discrepancy on Alex's own rule (D).
    24	- **No common, sourced product mechanism is found.** By D604's rule this closes the route to a candidate. The gate stays unmet; a
    25	  later candidate is not excluded.
    26	- **A number for Alex's question on the six lines' role, a reading of stored marks and not a change of any line.** Without XR, line
    27	  5 on the fresh topics would read 3 of 5 (unresolved for) or 2 of 5 (against). On the development map it would read 9 or 7 of 13
    28	  (`gate1-stick/RESULT.md`). In both cases the gate's line-5 outcome depends heavily on a mark the product does not use.
    29	- **Limits:** one week, one draw, 5 topics, control arm only. The XR readings are the recorded ones; I did not re-read the sources
    30	  for XR here.

